# Let's explore

## Creating correlation matrix


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
correlations <- brown_trout |>
  dplyr::select(Length_mm,
    Weight_g,
    Temperature_C,
    pH,
    Hardness,
    Conductivity,
    Flow,
    Elevation_ft)

GGally::ggpairs(
  correlations,
  upper = list(
    continuous = GGally::wrap("cor", size = 7)
  )
) +
  theme(
    text = element_text(size = 16),
    strip.text = element_text(size = 14),
    axis.text = element_text(size = 10)
  )
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](Trout_statistics_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-12-1.png){width=1920}
:::
:::


**Strong correlations to look at:**

- **Length vs Weight r = 0.774**
- **pH vs Conductivity r = 0.537**
- **Flow vs Elevation r = -0.797**
- **Temperature vs Elevation r = -0.728**

























